{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoGEdbYMSCZKGT6pW9Ps","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't run anything yet. This command is destructive, so I need your approval first.\n\n**Command:**\n```\nbq rm -r -f -d example-project-dev:staging_old\n```\n\n**What it does:**\n- `-d` targets the dataset `staging_old` in project `example-project-dev`.\n- `-r` deletes everything in the dataset: all tables, views, routines and models.\n- `-f` skips the confirmation prompt, so nothing will ask again.\n\n**Can it be undone?**\n- Not normally. After the dataset is deleted, its contents can't be restored with a standard command.\n- BigQuery time travel can sometimes restore *deleted tables* for up to the window set on the dataset (default 7 days). That only works if you recreate a dataset with the same name quickly. It isn't guaranteed.\n- Treat it as permanent.\n\nI haven't inspected the dataset. If you want, I can first list its tables and check last-modified times to confirm it really is the old staging copy, and that nothing still reads from it.\n\nReply \"yes\" to run the command as written. You can also ask me to check the dataset first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":942,"cache_read_input_tokens":19618,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":942},"output_tokens":358,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"599f6d1c-0bab-41a3-9ac0-340be30c9323","uuid":"569e9057-e1f4-469f-a911-68ad35e81029","timestamp":"2026-11-07T08:37:03.413Z","request_id":"req_011CgoGEdR8JAiga3CMZAwAU"}
